<title>USA: Clinton proposes $397 million in current year cuts.</title>
<headline>Clinton proposes $397 million in current year cuts.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton proposed to Congress Tuesday that $397 million in money appropriated for spending this year be rescinded.</p>
<p>In addition, Clinton proposed that $7 million in funds for the Social Security Administration be deferred.</p>
<p>The $397 million was allocated to the departments of Agriculture, Defense, Energy, Housing and Urban Development, and Justice, as well as the General Services Administration.</p>
<p>The Republican-led Congress must approve the budget rescissions and deferral.</p>
</text>
